 "poem": "FROM HER ROBING-SHIP - REV. JONAS A.\nO sweet old Tower of Judah! O,\nA tomb that bared the pillars above,\nAnd in those kings' eyes, thine is a glory,\nYet here beneath thee yet ne'er appears\nWhat glory was o'er thy towers before;\nFor all the rooms are full of evil things,\nWhich bring them back to their own evil.\nNor can I fancy what a glorious\nDay's blest aspect we'll see when our\nCrowns shall be coronated on our\nInstructive monument; and the people",
